[size=5][b]Every mod key and controller button, rebindable in the vanilla menu.[/b][/size]

The game only lets you rebind its own keyboard keys, and many mods keep theirs in input files or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], or hardcode them. Unified Keybinds adds a section per installed mod to [b]Settings > Controls > Key Bindings[/b], built from your mods at every startup, so you rebind everything in one place.

[i]Formerly Native Mod Keybinds. Files and folders keep their names, so updating works as before.[/i]

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]One section per mod with names from the mod's files, for example [i]"Mod: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url]"[/i] with [i]"Vehicle Flight Linear Brake"[/i]. Add or remove a mod and the sections follow.[/*]
[*]Also lists keys the mod didn't make rebindable, for example [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11765]Enhanced Vehicle System[/url]'s F1 to F4 and T. Actions already in the menu (vanilla, or from mods like [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4008]No More Hard-coded Keybinds[/url]) are not listed twice.[/*]
[*]A changed key applies right away and stays in sync with where the mod keeps it (see the table below).[/*]
[*]Key combinations show as their keys ([i]"F2 + 2"[/i]). Record your own: [b]hold one key and press another[/b] ([i]"Ctrl + K"[/i], [i]"Q + E"[/i]), or on a controller [b]hold one button and press another[/b] ([i]"LB + A"[/i]). A key pressed alone is bound alone. [b]Defaults[/b] restores a combination from the next launch.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/combination.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/prompt.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Tap or hold on one key[/b]: a (Hold) action can share its key with another action. Tap for the other action, hold for this one, for example [b]Sprint (Hold) and Dodge on B[/b], or Crouch (Hold) and Dodge/Dash on Mouse 4. The hold only counts on the device where the key is shared, so a lone Sprint (Hold) key stays instant.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/shared-key.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Controller rebinding[/b], which the game doesn't offer: with a controller in use, the menu shows controller buttons for mod actions, and switches back when you use the keyboard.[/*]
[*][b]Unbinding[/b], which the game doesn't offer: point at any entry and press [b]X[/b] (Square on a controller). It stays unbound across save loads and restarts, and [b]Defaults[/b] brings the key back. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11429]Allow Unbound Actions[/url] is no longer needed, and still works alongside.[/*]
[*]Optional file [b]Vanilla Controller Rebinding[/b]: vanilla controller buttons too, with the game's own names, following your control scheme (Classic, Dynamic, Alternative). The [b]Control Scheme[/b] screen shows your bindings. Sprint (Hold) and Crouch (Hold) get controller entries too.[/*]
[*]Never changes game or mod files, so mods that edit the settings menu keep working.[/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Supported keybind sources[/b][/size]

[table][tr][th]Status[/th]
[th]Keybind source[/th]
[th]Notes[/th]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] input file, with or without [font=Courier New]overridableUI[/font] (for example [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11765]Enhanced Vehicle System[/url])[/td]
[td]Listed at startup.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url] key option[/td]
[td]Kept in sync both ways. Key combinations stay in this menu only.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/td]
[td]Works like [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url]. Its hub key (F8) is kept in sync with RCF's Options.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url][/td]
[td]Single keys. Kept in sync both ways.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28308]Unified Mod Settings[/url][/td]
[td]Edits [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url] keys, so it follows those rows.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td]Mods that keep their keys in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url]'s hub, like the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28390]DigitalVixen[/url] mods ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/29105]Shattered Chrome[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/29101]Chrome Plating[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30508]Injuries[/url] and others)[/td]
[td]With the mod's own names. Single keys and controller buttons. Kept in sync both ways.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]⏳ Not yet[/b][/td]
[td]...[/td]
[td]If you notice a mod or framework that isn't mentioned here, [b]leave a comment[/b] and I'll look into supporting it.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]⏳ Not yet[/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] hotkeys ([font=Courier New]registerHotkey[/font], [font=Courier New]registerInput[/font])[/td]
[td]I'm still exploring a way to integrate these seamlessly.[/td]
[/tr]
[/table][size=4][b][color=#e5be37]Limitations[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Controller: an action is listed when exactly one button triggers it. Movement, aiming, attacking and stick axes stay as they are.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Controller: the game gives no warning when two actions share a button, and one of them may stop working.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]A new key combination or shared key applies after a restart (a popup tells you), and so does rebinding an action whose key and controller button were both unbound. Press the second key within half a second of the first. The game crashes with more than about 30 combinations in total, so past that an action keeps its key.[/b][/color]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/restart-popup.png[/img][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Controller combinations are recorded through XInput (Xbox controllers, others through Steam Input). A PlayStation controller on the game's own support may not record them.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]An action sharing a key with a (Hold) action stops reacting to holding that key on that device. A tap still works.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]A mod that registers its input file late through [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url]'s plugin interface may only appear from the second launch.[/b][/color][/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url][/*]
[*]Optional, for the keys kept there: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/*]
[/list][size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex, or extract into the game folder. The optional file goes on top of the main file. The files go to:
[code]red4ext/plugins/ModKeybindsMenu/
bin/x64/plugins/cyber_engine_tweaks/mods/ModKeybindsMenu/init.lua
red4ext/plugins/ModKeybindsMenu/scripts/ModKeybindsMenu/VanillaController.reds (optional file)[/code][size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
Remove both [font=Courier New]ModKeybindsMenu[/font] folders. Optionally delete [font=Courier New]r6/cache/modkeybinds/[/font], where the mod keys are kept. Nothing is written to your save. On 1.0.0, [b]start the game once with a newer version before uninstalling[/b], so your settings file gets cleaned up.

[size=4][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Your action shows up if an [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] file gives it [font=Courier New]<button id="IK_..." overridableUI="yourActionName" />[/font], or if it is a [font=Courier New]Button[/font] mapping with a single key or key combination ([font=Courier New]buttonGroup[/font]) and no [font=Courier New]overridableUI[/font], listed under the mapping's name.

For nicer names, ship [font=Courier New]r6/config/modkeybinds/<YourMod>.json[/font]:
[code]{
"_section": "Your Mod",
"yourActionName": "Open Menu"
}[/code][font=Courier New]_section[/font] names the section for every action in that file. Names can also be [font=Courier New]LocKey#...[/font] keys.

